--- fixed-point invariance re-run (killshot_fixedpoint.py, POST-FIX) ---
# killshot_fixedpoint.py had a real bug, fixed in this round: its SCALING
# CHECK divided loose-root movement by max(tight-root movement, 1e-300).
# Tight-root movement is legitimately EXACT 0.0 (step() short-circuits at
# k=0 whenever the root's own ||F||_max is already below step()'s Newton
# tol=1e-10 -- that is the T4 fix working, not an edge case). Dividing by
# ~1e-300 manufactured a ~1e296 ratio and tripped a false
# '>>> FLAG: possible leakage' line that directly contradicted the same
# file's own VERDICT section two lines later (PASS). Fixed by falling back
# to an absolute residual-scaled bar (identical to the VERDICT's own bar)
# whenever the tight-root movement is below a 1e-13 noise floor. No change
# to march_s.py: projectors/sign/no-eigenvalues constraints untouched --
# this was a diagnostic-script arithmetic bug, not a DAE/physics defect.
